# Python type checking

When a task creates or modifies Python files and `pyrefly` is available, run
`pyrefly check` before finishing. Fix the underlying type errors rather than
suppressing them. Do not expand the task to fix unrelated pre-existing errors
unless the user asks.

# Codex Delegation Policy

Before delegating ANY task to OpenAI Codex through the
`codex@openai-codex` plugin, Claude MUST perform a quota preflight.

## 1. Mandatory Preflight

- Check Codex account rate limits before invoking `/codex:rescue`.
- Use the authenticated Codex App Server rate-limit API:
  `account/rateLimits/read`.
- Check all available usage windows, including the 5-hour
  limit and weekly limit.
- Check server-side usage permission and reset timestamps.
- Do not assume that successful authentication means quota is available.

### sample script

codex 暂时没有提供用量查询接口。可以通过临时脚本进行 json-rpc over studio
```mjs
const proc = spawn("codex", ["app-server"], { stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe"] });

// 第一步：初始化握手
send({ id: 1, method: "initialize", params: {
  clientInfo: { name: "Claude Code", title: "Codex Plugin", version: "1.0.6" },
  capabilities: { experimentalApi: true, requestAttestation: false, optOutNotificationMethods: [] }
}});

// 收到 initialize 结果后：发已初始化通知，再查配额
send({ method: "initialized", params: {} });
send({ id: 2, method: "account/rateLimits/read", params: {} });
```

返回的数据结构（关键字段）：
- ordinaryUsageAllowed — 服务器是否允许普通使用
- rateLimits.primary — 5 小时窗口：usedPercent、windowDurationMins: 300、resetsAt（Unix 秒）
- rateLimits.secondary — 每周窗口：usedPercent、windowDurationMins: 10080、resetsAt
- rateLimits.credits / planType / spendControlReached
- rateLimitResetCredits — 可用的免费重置券
- accountId

## 2. Delegation Rules

- If all relevant usage windows have sufficient remaining quota,
  Codex delegation is allowed.
- If any relevant usage window has less than 15% remaining,
  avoid delegating non-essential tasks.
- If the server reports that ordinary usage is not allowed,
  do not delegate.
- If quota information cannot be retrieved, treat quota status
  as UNKNOWN and do not automatically delegate.

## 3. Fallback Strategy

When Codex quota is insufficient or unknown:

- Continue solving the task using Claude.
- Do not repeatedly retry Codex.
- Inform the user why Codex delegation was skipped.
- Include the latest known quota reset time when available.

## 4. Enforcement

- This policy applies to all Codex delegation methods,
  including `/codex:rescue` and `codex:codex-rescue`.
- Never bypass this preflight by directly invoking
  codex-companion.mjs.
- Never claim quota was checked unless an actual rate-limit
  response was successfully obtained.
- Do not modify the official Codex plugin source code.
